"question": "A biologist discovers two new animal species. Species X is a filter-feeding, sessile organism with no true tissues or body symmetry. Species Y has tentacles with stinging cells, a gastrovascular cavity, and a body plan that can be divided into mirror images along any plane through its central axis. How should these species be classified? \n\nSpecies X Body Plan: \n. . . . . . . \n. . irregular. . \n. . . shape. . . \n. . . . . . . . \nSpecies Y Body Plan: \n. . . .(*). . . .",
